<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article article-type="correction" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Gen Physiol</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of General Physiology</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0022-1295</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-7748</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2229400</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Correction</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title><italic>The Journal of General Physiology.</italic> Volume 110, No. 4,&#x02009; October 1997.  </article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Kontis</surname><given-names/></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>K.J.</surname><given-names/></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Rounaghi</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Goldin.</surname><given-names>A.L.</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>1</day><month>12</month><year>1997</year></pub-date><volume>110</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>763</fpage><lpage>763</lpage><copyright-year>1997</copyright-year><related-article related-article-type="corrected-article" vol="110" page="391" id="N0x1de3f30N0x40915f0" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="9379171" ext-link-type="pubmed"/></article-meta></front><body><sec><sec><title>Page 391.</title><p>Table <xref ref-type="table" rid="TIV">IV</xref> referred to previous data from Chen et al. (1996) concerning mutations in domain IV of the sodium channel. However, the numbering system for mutations in domain IV used by Chen et al. (1996) differed from that used  in this paper. Therefore, two mutants were labeled incorrectly. Mutant 4R1Q should have been termed 4R0Q, and  mutant 4R3Q should have been termed 4R2Q. The corrected table is reprinted below. <table-wrap position="anchor" id="TIV"><label>Table IV</label><caption><p>Summary of Charge-neutralizing Mutation Effects on Activation</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left">Mutant</th><th/><th>v<sub>1/2</sub> shift<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-150">&#x0002a;</xref></th><th/><th>z<sub>m</sub> change (e<sub>0</sub>)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-150">&#x0002a;</xref></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td/><td/><td><italic>mV</italic></td><td/><td/></tr><tr><td align="left">1R1Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-152">&#x02021;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;3.3</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;0.6</td></tr><tr><td align="left">1R1Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-153">&#x000a7;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;2.0</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">0.0</td></tr><tr><td align="left">1R2Q</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;1.0</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;0.4</td></tr><tr><td align="left">1R2Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-153">&#x000a7;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;8.0</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;1.8<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-155">&#x02016;</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">1R3Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-152">&#x02021;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;4.7<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;1.7<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">1R3Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-153">&#x000a7;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;12.0</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;1.5<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-155">&#x02016;</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">1K4Q</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;18.5<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;1.2<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">1K4Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-153">&#x000a7;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;19.0</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;0.9<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-155">&#x02016;</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">2R1Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-152">&#x02021;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;13.3<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;1.2<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">2R2Q</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;4.4<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;1.1<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">2R3Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-152">&#x02021;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;0.4<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;1.6<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">2K4Q</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;14.9<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;0.7</td></tr><tr><td align="left">2K5Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-153">&#x000a7;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;10.0</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">0.0</td></tr><tr><td align="left">3K1Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-152">&#x02021;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;10.4<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;0.5</td></tr><tr><td align="left">3R2Q</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;0.3</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;0.4</td></tr><tr><td align="left">3R3Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-152">&#x02021;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;5.9<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;2.1<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">3R4Q</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;18.1<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;0.3</td></tr><tr><td align="left">4R0Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-152">&#x02021;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;2.3</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;1.6<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">4R2Q</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;3.6<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;0.5</td></tr><tr><td align="left">4R2Q<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-152">&#x02021;</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;8.6<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x02212;1.6<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TFIV-176">176</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left">4R4Q</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;0.4</td><td align="left"/><td align="left">&#x0002b;0.9</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="TFIV-150"><label>&#x0002a;</label><p>v<sub>1/2</sub> and z<sub>m</sub> are the half-maximal voltage and gating valence of activation.  Data from St&#x000fc;hmer et al. (1989) did not include an assessment of statistical significance. &#x000a0;</p></fn><fn id="TFIV-152"><label>&#x02021;</label><p>Data from Chen et al. (1996). &#x000a0;</p></fn><fn id="TFIV-153"><label>&#x000a7;</label><p>Data from St&#x000fc;hmer et al.  (1989). &#x000a0;</p></fn><fn id="TFIV-155"><label>&#x02016;</label><p>The values for z<sub>m</sub> from St&#x000fc;hmer et al. (1989) were multiplied by  three for comparison because those values were based on three identical  gating charges (m<sup>3</sup>). &#x000a0;</p></fn><fn id="TFIV-176"><label>176</label><p>Values statistically significant, with a probability &#x0003c;0.05  resulting from random variation.    &#x000a0;</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></p></sec></sec></body></article>